## PR Context in Agent

### Automatic PR Detection

When Cursor detects you're on a branch with an open PR:

1. Fetches the PR diff (`git diff base...HEAD`)
2. Fetches PR metadata (title, description, reviewers)
3. Fetches review comments (if authenticated with GitHub/GitLab)
4. Fetches CI status (if connected to CI/CD)

The agent then has full PR context:

- "This is PR #42 for the OAuth2 feature, opened against main"
- "Reviewer @alice requested changes to the callback handler"
- "CI checks are passing: lint, test, build"

### PR-Focused Agent Commands

```
# Ask agent to review PR
"Review this PR and suggest improvements"

# Ask agent to address review feedback
"Fix the issues mentioned in @alice's review comments"

# Ask agent to update PR description
"Generate a detailed PR description for these changes"

# Ask agent to check PR CI
"What CI checks are running on this PR?"
```

### PR Generation Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Dev as Developer
    participant IDE as Cursor IDE
    participant Agent as AI Agent
    participant Git as Git Remote
    
    Dev->>IDE: Open Composer on feature branch
    IDE->>Agent: Provide branch context
    Agent->>Git: Fetch PR list
    Git-->>Agent: Return open PRs
    Agent->>Git: Fetch PR diff
    Git-->>Agent: Return PR changes
    Agent->>Agent: Analyze diff + comments
    Agent-->>Dev: PR summary + review suggestions
    Dev->>Agent: "Update PR description"
    Agent->>IDE: Write updated PR description
```

