## Multi-Branch Workflows

### Switching Context Between Branches

```bash
# Agent can help understand branch differences
"Show me the differences between feature/oauth and main"
"List files changed in feature/oauth since it diverged from main"

# Agent analyzes:
git diff main...feature/oauth
# → Returns list of changed files and diff summary
```

### Feature Branch Pattern

```
1. Create branch: git checkout -b feature/add-search
2. Work on feature: Edit files, test changes
3. Agent generates commits: "Stage and commit these changes"
4. Push branch: git push -u origin feature/add-search
5. Create PR: Agent or manual via GitHub/GitLab
6. Review: Agent can review PR comments
7. Merge: Agent can prepare merge commit
```

### Agent in Feature Branches

When working in a feature branch, the agent:

- Uses branch name to infer task type (feat/fix/docs)
- Adjusts commit message types automatically
- Considers branch history when generating code
- References PR context when available

