## Commit Attribution

### How Agent Commits Are Attributed

| Source | Author | Committer |
|--------|--------|-----------|
| **Manual commit** | Your git identity | Your git identity |
| **Agent via Composer** | Your git identity | Your git identity |
| **Agent via Claude Code CLI** | Your git identity (if configured) | Your git identity |
| **Agent via Automations (cloud)** | `cursor-automation` | `cursor-automation` |

### Configuring Agent Commit Identity

```bash
# Set global git identity for AI commits
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your@email.com"

# Or set per-repo
git config user.name "Your Name"
git config user.email "your@email.com"

# Use in Claude Code CLI
claude --git-author "AI Assistant <ai@cursor.com>" "Generate and commit these changes"
```

### Cloud Agent PR Attribution

When Cloud Agent creates a PR:

```
PR Author: cursor-automation (<team>@cursor.com)
Branch: cursor-automation/feature/<run-id>
Commit message: Generated by Cursor Cloud Agent

Example:
Author: cursor-automation <team@cursor.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 11 10:00:00 2026 +0000

    feat(auth): add OAuth2 login flow

    Implements Google OAuth2 login flow including:
    - Google provider configuration
    - OAuth2 callback handler
    - Token validation middleware
    - Unit tests for all new functions
```

